                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 8,
                            "last_played": 1517098711
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "It's early.  Like, early early.  Like unplayable, no direction, can't access options menu, raw scraps off the cutting room floor early.  Here's a blatant lie from the developer on the Steam Early access description: “Batch 17 is very near feature completion, and the three additional worlds which consist of the remainder of the work have already been completed and are now being polished. We anticipate this process taking 2-3 months.”  After a series of 'a little too early for early access' games coming out lately, this one really takes the cake and feels not only incomplete beyond what's reasonable, but plain old insulting to the consumer.",
                        "timestamp_created": 1517098794,
                        "timestamp_updated": 1517544137,
                        "voted_up": false,
                        "votes_up": 24,
                        "votes_funny": 7,
                        "weighted_vote_score": 0.6765519380569458,
                        "comment_count": 8,
                        "steam_purchase": true,
                        "received_for_free": false,
                        "written_during_early_access": true,
                        "developer_response": "Hi Ori,\n\nI want to apologize again for your experience.  You were absolutely right in your initial assessment that the game was raw.  It still is, and I completely agree.  We really messed up how we introduce players to the game, and have some real issues with direction in the game.\n\nI want to reiterate, that we welcome that feedback, and again, sincerely apologize.  \n\nI do also want to say, with regards to the other reviews of the game, they are absolutely just fans of the game. They purchased the game after beta testing it for months and just wanted to leave very glowing reviews.  Let me say, from a purely business perspective, were one to suggest to anyone that they review their own game, one might suggest they tone it down to something more reasonable like \"Game ran for 8 minutes without crashing, 6/10\" .  \n\nAlso, with regards to shady tactics or cash grabs - anyone who can guess our sales numbers knows that's a hilarious statement.  Further, I'm not even trying to find new players until we fix the experience for people, or else we just get more negative reviews.  \n\nI know we lost you as a player, and I completely understand.  I also think you are trying to do a really good thing warning people off of scams, etc. But there's no cash grab here.  We haven't sold anywhere close to 3 digits of players.\n\nAt this point, we are only doing this to make a fun game for ourselves and the people who do actually play.",
